+# Boulder 1.02 on HarmonyOS PC
+
+This project hosts the original Boulder C++ game and map editor in ArkUI
+XComponent surfaces. Conan builds both NAPI modules against SDL2 2.32.10 and
+places the modules and the matching SDK C++ runtime in `entry/libs/arm64-v8a`.
+The SDK runtime notice is retained in `licenses/ohos-native-runtime`. The app
+namespace cannot rely on the shell's system copy of libc++_shared.so.
+Game rules, rendering, level data,
+audio decoding and map editing remain upstream code. The adaptation supplies
+window lifecycle, input forwarding and application sandbox paths.
+
+Copy the installed `share/boulder/harmony-project` directory to a writable
+directory. Open it in DevEco Studio, install its local module dependencies, and
+configure your own debug signing for the default product. Build and install
+`entry-default-signed.hap` on your device. No account, signing certificate,
+password or provision profile is included. Tested host SDK: HarmonyOS 6.0.2(22),
+arm64-v8a; native libraries are built with the contest's OHOS clang 15 profile.
+
+The home screen opens the game or map editor. Enter starts a selected level;
+arrow keys move. In the editor select a tile and click the map, S saves and L
+reloads `newlevel.map`, F1-F5 change the brush size. Saved maps and high scores
+live in the application files directory. The original game enumerates custom
+maps from that directory. Bundled assets live under `files/data`.
+
+The surface currently uses the upstream 1024x768 pixel canvas. The host adds no
+system desktop overlay and does not require a Broadway or X11 server. A raw
+SSH process has no native application surface; use the HAP for graphical play.
+
+`boulder-check assets DATA_DIR` runs the original decoders and map loader.
+`boulder-check roundtrip DATA_DIR NEW_MAP` exercises original editor save/load.
+These checks do not substitute for real display, input and audible music tests.
